WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.400
Take the whole parabola
y equals x squared,

2
00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:06.490
and reflect it in the line y equals x.

3
00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:10.370
The mirror image is the same
parabola, lying on its side.

4
00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:14.440
Yet before finding an inverse,
mathematicians chop off half,

5
00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:17.210
keeping only x of nought or more.

6
00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:20.910
Why must y equals x squared
lose half its domain?

7
00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:23.520
Because negative numbers can't be squared?

8
00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:26.350
In this mission, you'll meet
the inverse of a function,

9
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.230
which undoes the function.

10
00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:33.130
Its graph is the reflection of the
original graph in the line y equals x.

11
00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:37.700
And you'll build composite functions,
and sketch the modulus function.

12
00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:42.930
Your mission: explain why y equals x
squared must lose half its domain before

13
00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:44.120
it has an inverse.
